## 1. Review & Understand the Task

- Keep legacy ```` ```lang path ```` fences as fallback — `codeBlockExtractor.js` already does this; no change needed there.
- Extend the **markdown parsing/rendering layer** so both syntaxes become renderable blocks:
  - old: ```` ```lang path/to/file … ``` ````
  - new: `<file_change path="…" language="…" change_type="…" encoding="text"> … <file_change/>`
- Files to inspect: `src/utils/markdownParser.js`, `src/components/document/Document.vue`, `MarkdownViewer.vue`, and anything rendering blocks.

Let me gather the actual code before proposing changes.

## 2. Information Gathering## 1. Review & Understand the Task

- The XML envelope `<file_change …> … <file_change/>` must be understood by the **document rendering stack**, while the legacy ```` ```lang path ```` fences stay supported as fallback.
- Current state found on disk:
  - `src/utils/markdownParser.js` still parses the **old `@@ CODX_FILE @@` sentinel** syntax (not the XML envelope). This is the file that feeds `Document.vue` → `ChapterBlock` → `Code`/`MarkdownViewer`.
  - `src/components/document/Document.vue` has no parser of its own — it delegates to `parser.parseChapters()` / `parser.parseBlocks()`, so fixing the parser fixes Document.
  - `src/components/MarkdownViewer.vue` renders markdown with `markdown-it` (`html: true`) and would leak a raw `<file_change …>` envelope as HTML instead of a code block.
  - `src/components/document/DocumentSummary.vue` builds the TOC by scanning ```` ```lang path ```` fence lines only.

## 2. Information Gathering (summary)

| File | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `src/utils/markdownParser.js` | Single source of truth for blocks/chapters. Contains CODX sentinel parsing (`getCodedFileMarkers`, `parseCodedFileMetaLine`, `parseCodedFileBlock`) + `isInsideCodeFence` guard used by `parseChapters`/`parseChapter`. |
| `src/components/document/Document.vue` | Uses `parser.parseChapters` + `parser.parseBlocks` only → inherits new syntax. |
| `src/components/document/ChapterBlock.vue` | `isCodeBlock(block) { return !!block.fileName || block.isFileBlock === true }` → already renders envelope blocks as code. |
| `src/components/MarkdownViewer.vue` | `sanitizedText` → `md.render()`. Needs envelope→fence normalization. |
| `src/components/document/DocumentSummary.vue` | Own fence scanner for TOC entries. Needs envelope awareness. |

No other consumers of `getCodedFileMarkers` / `parseCodedFileBlock` exist, so replacing them is self-contained.

## 3. Change Proposal

1. **`markdownParser.js`**
   - Drop the `@@ CODX_* @@` helpers.
   - Add `<file_change …>` helpers: `getFileChangeOpenTag` (returns parsed attributes or `null`), `isFileChangeCloseTag` (`<file_change/>`, `<file_change />`, `</file_change>`, `</file_change />`), `parseFileChangeAttributes` (`key="value"` **and** `key"value"`), `parseFileChangeBlock` (verbatim body, streaming-friendly).
   - `isInsideCodeFence()` also skips envelope bodies so `#` lines inside a file body never become chapters.
   - `parseBlocks()` parses envelopes first (when not inside a legacy fence) and emits `{ type, content, fileName, filePath, renderer, finished, isFileBlock, fileChangeType, encoding }`.
   - New `fileChangeBlocksToFences(content)` helper: rewrites envelopes into standard fences (fence length adapts to nested backticks) so any markdown renderer displays them.
   - Legacy ```` ```lang path ```` branch untouched.
2. **`MarkdownViewer.vue`** — normalize envelopes to fences in `sanitizedText` (before `md.render`), so highlighting + `code-block-anchor` generation work identically for both syntaxes.
3. **`DocumentSummary.vue`** — envelope opening tag becomes a TOC entry (path → same anchor slug as fences); body is skipped.
4. **`Document.vue` / `ChapterBlock.vue`** — no code change required (parser-driven, `isFileBlock`/`fileName` already supported).

Risks / edge cases:
- A literal `<file_change/>` line inside a body terminates the block (documented in the helper comments).
- Opening tag attributes must stay on the same line.
- Unterminated (streaming) envelope yields partial content and `finished: false`.

## 4. Changes Summary

| File | Change |
